# Scrumban — QA & Release Gates

> **Authority boundary:** This rule documents procedures and gates only; it never grants execution authorization for remote operations.

## Required Authorizations (Never Implicit)

- Remote Preview/DEV flag writes & deploys: explicit branch/SHA-scoped authorization
- Integrated suite (`--execute` against DEV): `R3_INTEGRATED_AUTH=AUTH-R3-INTEGRATED`
- Independent Rollback OFF (`--apply`): `R3_ROLLBACK_AUTH=AUTH-R3-ROLLBACK-OFF`
- Any Production write (flags, SQL migration, merge to `main`, deploy): explicit Production window authorization

## Canonical QA Commands (Local & Authorized Preview/DEV)

- Local harness & anti-Prod guards: `npm run qa:r3:test` and `node --test scripts/qa/qaGuard.test.mjs`
- Preflight (read-only, requires 9/9 READY): `npm run qa:r3:preflight`
- Integrated suite (R3-I0..I7, requires explicit auth + `R3_EXPECTED_SHA` + `R3_EXPECTED_BRANCH`): `npm run qa:r3:integrated -- --execute`
- Independent Rollback OFF (always run in try/finally after ON window): `npm run qa:r3:rollback -- --apply`

## Mandatory GO / NO-GO Criteria

- **Release Candidate VALIDATED** requires: OFF + legacy smoke PASS, `R1_ONLY` PASS, ON + `R3-I0..I7` 8/8 PASS, cleanup (`remainingMemory=0`, `remainingDocuments=0`, `errors=[]`), Rollback OFF PASS, final Preflight OFF 9/9 READY, exact SHA & branch verified, R2 disabled.
- **Fail-closed:** Any mismatch in SHA, branch, target, or Supabase ref aborts immediately with zero writes.
- **Production:** Never insert fixtures or create QA users in Production.

## Evidence & Traceability

- Store sanitized JSON evidence under `.qa/` (gitignored), keyed by SHA and `runId`.
- Never overwrite historical candidate evidence; archive snapshots before updating latest pointers.
- Reuse valid evidence when `HEAD^{tree}` is unchanged; do not re-run full suites unnecessarily.
